.policy "celery-practice-unknown-task-name" revision 1
.description "Name Celery tasks by strings that match a registered task; a worker discards messages for unknown names, so a mistyped beat entry never runs."
.language python
.mode log
.scope include "**/*.py"
// Rerail's own rule, not a port. Celery sends only a task's name; the worker looks it up in its registry, and for a
// name no task registered it logs "Received unregistered task of type ..." and discards the message
// (celery/worker/consumer/consumer.py, UNKNOWN_TASK_ERROR). A beat entry whose "task" has a typo, or names a task that
// was renamed or moved to another module, is sent on schedule and dropped every time: the job silently never runs.
// Reported, at the naming site, when no task of the run is registered under the name and the run owns it:
//   - the first argument (or `name=`) of `send_task(...)` on a Celery app (lib/celery's cel_app_ref or cel_app_value:
//     a resolved app, a factory's result, current_app, `self.app`), of celery's `signature(...)` and of
//     `<app>.signature(...)`;
//   - the "task" of a beat schedule entry: a dict (a literal or `dict(...)`) with a "task" and a "schedule" key
//     (Celery's documented entry shape), or with a "task" and an "options" key when its value reaches the beat
//     setting: it lies in a beat_schedule setting's value (lib/celery's cel_setting), in an item assigned to or an
//     `.update(...)` of that setting, in a module constant one of those reads (through imports, `**` splats
//     included), or in a run function such a value calls, or one it reaches through the call graph (paperless-ngx
//     lists its entries with "options" in `parse_beat_schedule()` and adds each cron from the environment).
// The name is a string literal, or a constant the engine resolves: a module constant of the run (through imports,
// re-exports and module aliases), a class attribute (`ExportTask.name`) or a local of its function, each bound once.
// A task is registered under its `name=` (such a value), else under <module>.<def>, which a string matches also by a
// dotted tail; `app.task(fn)` and `shared_task(name=...)(fn)` called as functions register the same way. A class
// deriving from celery's Task (through the run's classes, or `<app>.Task`) is registered under its `name = ...`
// attribute (such a value), else <module>.<Class>; a class whose `name` does not resolve registers nothing. The run
// owns a name n when n's module part (before the last dot) is exactly a module of the run, or when the run registers
// tasks under explicit dotted names that share n's first segment (`name="reports.scheduler"`). When a task with n's
// last segment as its def name exists elsewhere (a moved task), the message names it.
//   "task": "proj.tasks.shipp"          reported (proj/tasks.py defines `ship`)
//   app.send_task("proj.tasks.ship")    not reported (`@shared_task def ship` in proj/tasks.py)
//   app.send_task("billing.charge")     not reported (no module `billing` in the run: another service's task)
//   remote.send_task("tasks.upload")    not reported (the run has `proj/tasks.py`, but no module `tasks`)
//   ML_JOBS = [{"task": "proj.x.y", "options": {...}}]   not reported (never reaches the beat setting)
// Left alone: Celery's own tasks (`celery.*`, the names celery/app/builtins.py registers; the one name list kept,
// since a run module named `celery` would otherwise own them); a library's tasks (`django_celery_beat.*`), unowned
// unless the library is part of the run, where its tasks are registered; names whose module part is not a module of
// the run and whose first segment no explicit task name shares (another service's tasks: send_task is often used
// exactly for that); `send_task` on an object that is no Celery app; names built at runtime (f-strings, parameters,
// constants bound more than once); commented-out entries; test code (cel_test_doc).
// Gaps: tasks registered by a decorator wrapper that computes the name; a task name held by a constant outside the run;
// task modules autodiscovered from outside the run (an installed package); a run whose module names carry an extra
// leading package the worker does not (`api.tasks.x`, which the worker imports as `tasks.x`) does not own `tasks.*`;
// beat entries an app builds at runtime (`add_periodic_task`, django_celery_beat's PeriodicTask rows); whether the
// worker actually imports the module that defines the task (`include`/`imports`/autodiscover) is not checked.

#include "lib/celery.rerail"

.violation UnknownTaskName(at: node, n: symbol) "No task in this code registers \"{n}\", so a worker would discard it. Check it against the worker's registered tasks; leave it if another service or an installed package registers it."
UnknownTaskName(at, n) :- uk_unknown(at, n), !uk_moved(n, _).
.violation MovedTaskName(at: node, n: symbol, q: symbol) "No task registers \"{n}\"; a task \"{q}\" has its function name, so it may have moved. Check the worker's registered tasks; leave it if another service or a package registers it."
MovedTaskName(at, n, q) :- uk_unknown(at, n), uk_moved(n, q).

.decl uk_unknown(at: node, n: symbol)
uk_unknown(at, n) :- uk_ref(at, n), !uk_known(n), uk_owned(n), !uk_celery_own(n), docof(at, d), !cel_test_doc(d).

// ---- values ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// uk_str_value(v, n): v is the string n, or a name or attribute resolving to a constant bound once to it: a module
// constant of the run (cel_sym follows imports, re-exports and module aliases), a class attribute (`Cls.name`), or a
// local name of its own function.
.decl uk_str_value(v: node, n: symbol)
uk_str_value(v, n) :- str(v, n).
uk_str_value(v, n) :- unparen(v, u), (kind(u, "identifier") ; kind(u, "attribute")), cel_sym(u, q), uk_const(q, n).
uk_str_value(v, n) :- unparen(v, u), kind(u, "identifier"), text(u, x), look(u, x, s), !kind(s, "module"),
    asg(s, x, w, _), str(w, n), count : { asg(s, x, _, _) } = 1.
.decl uk_const(q: symbol, n: symbol)
uk_const(q, n) :- cel_module_var(q, w), str(w, n), count : { cel_module_var(q, _) } = 1.
uk_const(q, n) :- split_dot(q, cq, x), class_def(c, cq), asg(c, x, w, _), str(w, n), count : { asg(c, x, _, _) } = 1.

// ---- the names the run uses --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// uk_site(e, how): expression e is where a task is named: send_task's first argument or `name=`, signature's first
// argument, a beat entry's "task".
.decl uk_site(e: node, how: symbol)
uk_site(e, "send_task") :- kind(c, "call"), field(c, "function", fn), attr_of(fn, o, "send_task"), unparen(o, u),
    (cel_app_ref(u) ; cel_app_value(u)), (posarg(c, 0, e) ; call_arg(c, -1, "name", e)).
uk_site(e, "signature") :- kind(c, "call"), field(c, "function", fn), sym_of(fn, q),
    (q = "celery.signature" ; q = "celery.canvas.signature" ; q = "celery.canvas.Signature" ; q = "celery.Signature" ;
    q = "celery.subtask" ; q = "celery.canvas.subtask"),
    posarg(c, 0, e).
uk_site(e, "signature") :- kind(c, "call"), field(c, "function", fn), attr_of(fn, o, "signature"), unparen(o, u),
    (cel_app_ref(u) ; cel_app_value(u)), posarg(c, 0, e).
uk_site(e, "beat") :- uk_entry_key(m, "task", e), uk_entry_key(m, "schedule", _).
uk_site(e, "beat") :- uk_entry_key(m, "task", e), uk_entry_key(m, "options", _), uk_beat_part(m).
// uk_entry_key(m, k, v): m is a dict literal with the string key k, or a `dict(...)` call with the keyword k; v its
// value.
.decl uk_entry_key(m: node, k: symbol, v: node)
uk_entry_key(m, k, v) :- kind(m, "dictionary"), child(m, p, _), kind(p, "pair"), field(p, "key", kn), str(kn, k),
    field(p, "value", v).
uk_entry_key(m, k, v) :- kind(m, "call"), field(m, "function", f), builtin_ref(f, "dict"), call_arg(m, -1, k, v).
// ---- what reaches the beat setting -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// uk_beat_expr(e): e's value reaches the beat setting: a beat_schedule setting's value, the value of an item assigned
// to the setting or of its `.update(...)`, a module constant read in a beat expression or in a beat function.
.decl uk_beat_expr(e: node)
uk_beat_expr(u) :- cel_setting("beat_schedule", v, _), unparen(v, u).
uk_beat_expr(u) :- kind(a, "assignment"), field(a, "left", l), kind(l, "subscript"), field(l, "value", t),
    uk_beat_target(t), field(a, "right", v), unparen(v, u).
uk_beat_expr(u) :- kind(c, "call"), field(c, "function", f), attr_of(f, t, "update"), uk_beat_target(t),
    call_arg(c, _, _, v), unparen(v, u).
uk_beat_expr(u) :- uk_beat_read(r), (kind(r, "identifier") ; kind(r, "attribute")), cel_sym(r, q),
    cel_module_var(q, w), unparen(w, u).
// uk_beat_read(r): r is a beat expression or lies in one, or lies in a beat function.
.decl uk_beat_read(r: node)
uk_beat_read(e) :- uk_beat_expr(e).
uk_beat_read(r) :- uk_beat_expr(e), within(r, e).
uk_beat_read(r) :- uk_beat_fn(g), within(r, g).
// uk_beat_fn(g): a run function whose result reaches the beat setting: called in a beat expression
// (`CELERY_BEAT_SCHEDULE = parse_beat_schedule()`), or reached from one through the call graph.
.decl uk_beat_fn(g: node)
uk_beat_fn(g) :- uk_beat_expr(e), uk_beat_call(e, g).
uk_beat_fn(g) :- uk_beat_expr(e), within(c, e), uk_beat_call(c, g).
uk_beat_fn(h) :- uk_beat_fn(g), reach(g, h).
.decl uk_beat_call(c: node, g: node)
uk_beat_call(c, g) :- kind(c, "call"), field(c, "function", f), cel_sym(f, q), qualname(g, q),
    kind(g, "function_definition").
// uk_beat_target(t): t is the beat setting: `<x>.conf.beat_schedule`, or a name bound to a beat expression
// (`CELERY_BEAT_SCHEDULE`, a celeryconfig's `beat_schedule`).
.decl uk_beat_target(t: node)
uk_beat_target(t) :- attr_of(t, o, "beat_schedule"), attr_of(o, _, "conf").
uk_beat_target(t) :- (kind(t, "identifier") ; kind(t, "attribute")), cel_sym(t, q), cel_module_var(q, w),
    unparen(w, u), uk_beat_expr(u).
// uk_beat_part(m): dict m reaches the beat setting.
.decl uk_beat_part(m: node)
uk_beat_part(m) :- uk_entry_key(m, "options", _), uk_beat_read(m).
// uk_ref(e, n): site e names the task n.
.decl uk_ref(e: node, n: symbol)
uk_ref(e, n) :- uk_site(e, _), uk_str_value(e, n).

// ---- the names the run registers ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// uk_reg(n, how): a task of the run is registered as n, "explicit" (a name= or a class's name attribute) or "implicit"
// (<module>.<def>, <module>.<Class>).
.decl uk_reg(n: symbol, how: symbol)
uk_reg(n, "explicit") :- cel_task_option(_, "name", v), uk_str_value(v, n).
uk_reg(n, "implicit") :- cel_task_name(f, n), !cel_task_option(f, "name", _).
// `app.task(fn)`, `app.task(fn, name=...)`, `shared_task(name=...)(fn)` called as functions.
uk_reg(n, "explicit") :- uk_wrap_call(c, _), uk_wrap_name(c, v), uk_str_value(v, n).
uk_reg(q, "implicit") :- uk_wrap_call(c, g), !uk_wrap_name(c, _), qualname(g, q).
.decl uk_wrap_call(c: node, g: node)
uk_wrap_call(c, g) :- kind(c, "call"), field(c, "function", fn), cel_task_fn(fn), posarg(c, 0, a), cel_sym(a, q),
    qualname(g, q), kind(g, "function_definition").
uk_wrap_call(c, g) :- kind(c, "call"), field(c, "function", k), kind(k, "call"), field(k, "function", fn),
    cel_task_fn(fn), posarg(c, 0, a), cel_sym(a, q), qualname(g, q), kind(g, "function_definition").
.decl uk_wrap_name(c: node, v: node)
uk_wrap_name(c, v) :- uk_wrap_call(c, _), call_arg(c, -1, "name", v).
uk_wrap_name(c, v) :- uk_wrap_call(c, _), field(c, "function", k), kind(k, "call"), call_arg(k, -1, "name", v).
uk_reg(n, "explicit") :- uk_task_class(c), uk_class_name_attr(c, v), uk_str_value(v, n).
uk_reg(@dot(mq, x), "implicit") :- uk_task_class(c), !uk_class_name_attr(c, _), def_name(c, x), docof(c, d),
    doc(d, _, mq), mq != "", nearest(c, m, scope), kind(m, "module").
.decl uk_known(n: symbol)
uk_known(n) :- uk_ref(_, n), uk_reg(n, _).
uk_known(n) :- uk_ref(_, n), uk_reg(q, "implicit"), suffix(cat(".", n), q).
// uk_task_class(c): c derives from celery's Task, directly, through `<app>.Task`, or through the run's classes.
.decl uk_task_class_q(q: symbol)
uk_task_class_q("celery.Task"). uk_task_class_q("celery.app.task.Task").
uk_task_class_q(q) :- uk_task_class(c), class_def(c, q).
.decl uk_task_class(c: node)
uk_task_class(c) :- kind(c, "class_definition"), cel_class_base(c, b), uk_task_class_q(b).
uk_task_class(c) :- kind(c, "class_definition"), field(c, "superclasses", al), child(al, e, _), attr_of(e, o, "Task"),
    unparen(o, u), (cel_app_ref(u) ; cel_app_value(u)).
// uk_class_name_attr(c, v): `name = v` in c's body (any value: one that does not resolve registers no implicit name).
.decl uk_class_name_attr(c: node, v: node)
uk_class_name_attr(c, v) :- kind(c, "class_definition"), field(c, "body", b), body_stmt(b, s, _),
    kind(s, "expression_statement"), child(s, a, 0), kind(a, "assignment"), field(a, "left", l), text(l, "name"),
    field(a, "right", v).

// ---- ownership ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// uk_owned(n): n's module part is exactly a module of the run, or n's first segment is shared by an explicit dotted
// name. A module that merely ends with n's module part (`app.tasks` for `tasks.x`) does not own it: another service's
// worker may well have a top-level `tasks` module.
.decl uk_owned(n: symbol)
uk_owned(n) :- uk_ref(_, n), split_dot(n, m, _), m != "", doc(_, _, m).
uk_owned(n) :- uk_ref(_, n), split_dot(n, m, _), m != "", h = @head(n), uk_reg(x, "explicit"), x != h, @head(x) = h.
// uk_celery_own(n): Celery's own tasks (celery/app/builtins.py registers them as `celery.*`).
.decl uk_celery_own(n: symbol)
uk_celery_own(n) :- uk_ref(_, n), @head(n) = "celery".
// uk_moved(n, q): a task whose def is named for n's last segment is registered as q.
.decl uk_moved(n: symbol, q: symbol)
uk_moved(n, q) :- uk_ref(_, n), split_dot(n, _, x), cel_task(f), def_name(f, x), cel_task_name(f, q), q != n.

// The cases, `cases/celery-practice-unknown-task-name/`: one repository in which each line ending in `# caught` is
// reported and no other line.
.test cases exactly
    .fixture "proj/__init__.py" from "../cases/celery-practice-unknown-task-name/proj/__init__.py"
    .fixture "proj/celery.py" from "../cases/celery-practice-unknown-task-name/proj/celery.py"
    .fixture "proj/classes.py" from "../cases/celery-practice-unknown-task-name/proj/classes.py"
    .fixture "proj/client.py" from "../cases/celery-practice-unknown-task-name/proj/client.py"
    .fixture "proj/contract.py" from "../cases/celery-practice-unknown-task-name/proj/contract.py"
    .fixture "proj/factory.py" from "../cases/celery-practice-unknown-task-name/proj/factory.py"
    .fixture "proj/jobs.py" from "../cases/celery-practice-unknown-task-name/proj/jobs.py"
    .fixture "proj/maintenance.py" from "../cases/celery-practice-unknown-task-name/proj/maintenance.py"
    .fixture "proj/metrics.py" from "../cases/celery-practice-unknown-task-name/proj/metrics.py"
    .fixture "proj/schedule.py" from "../cases/celery-practice-unknown-task-name/proj/schedule.py"
    .fixture "proj/settings.py" from "../cases/celery-practice-unknown-task-name/proj/settings.py"
    .fixture "proj/tasks.py" from "../cases/celery-practice-unknown-task-name/proj/tasks.py"
    .fixture "proj/tests/__init__.py" from "../cases/celery-practice-unknown-task-name/proj/tests/__init__.py"
    .fixture "proj/tests/test_beat.py" from "../cases/celery-practice-unknown-task-name/proj/tests/test_beat.py"
    .fixture "proj/web/__init__.py" from "../cases/celery-practice-unknown-task-name/proj/web/__init__.py"
    .fixture "proj/web/views.py" from "../cases/celery-practice-unknown-task-name/proj/web/views.py"
    .fixture "proj/worker.py" from "../cases/celery-practice-unknown-task-name/proj/worker.py"
    .expect _ at "proj/celery.py":10
    .expect _ at "proj/celery.py":11
    .expect _ at "proj/celery.py":19
    .expect _ at "proj/celery.py":23
    .expect _ at "proj/celery.py":35
    .expect _ at "proj/celery.py":73
    .expect _ at "proj/celery.py":80
    .expect _ at "proj/celery.py":91
    .expect _ at "proj/celery.py":94
    .expect _ at "proj/classes.py":14
    .expect _ at "proj/client.py":23
    .expect _ at "proj/client.py":24
    .expect _ at "proj/schedule.py":8
    .expect _ at "proj/schedule.py":16
    .expect _ at "proj/settings.py":4
    .expect _ at "proj/web/views.py":14
    .expect _ at "proj/web/views.py":15
    .expect _ at "proj/web/views.py":16
    .expect _ at "proj/web/views.py":22
    .expect _ at "proj/web/views.py":24
    .expect _ at "proj/web/views.py":28
    .expect _ at "proj/web/views.py":29
    .expect _ at "proj/web/views.py":33
.end
